  "description": "Shared vectors for the object-prefix layout: a table with an object-prefix field keeps every data file and deletion vector under <data_path>/data/<ns>/<table>/<field>=<value>/, where value is the canonical decimal of the file's identity partition value. prefix_cases: build the prefix, or refuse the value. containment_cases: whether a path is an object under a prefix. stats_cases: whether a file's column stats for the field prove every row holds the value (Iceberg single-value bounds, lowercase hex). iam: resource_pattern with the tag replaced by each of values must equal 'arn:aws:s3:::' + that value's prefix without 's3://' + '*'; read as an IAM glob ('*' spans '/'), the pattern for value 4 must not match 'arn:aws:s3:::' + each of foreign_keys (bucket/key strings). The count of every case, iam values and foreign keys included, is pinned by the server's ObjectPrefixVectorsTest and by pyhoglake's test_object_prefix_vectors.py.",
